<%
# ggen_igniter EEx template -> docs/reference/types/<record_name>.md
#
# --for-each fan-out, transplanted from xaas's real, proven N-way
# render pattern (docs/claude/diataxis/how-to/fix-ash-admin-and-use-ggen-for-codegen.md's
# "Real N-way fan-out from one invocation" section, 44 real files from one
# invocation). One focused reference page per admitted bpm:RecordType
# individual, instead of every type crammed into a single monolithic
# docs/reference/beam4pm_types_reference.md.
#
# Bindings: `record_name`/`record_doc` (this row, flattened, from the
# --for-each `records` query); `fields` (the FULL fields.rq result list,
# every record's fields -- build_bindings/2 binds every named query's full
# row-list regardless of for-each, so the fields for THIS record are
# filtered out of the full list here rather than needing a second
# --for-each pass).
this_record_fields =
  fields
  |> Enum.filter(fn f -> f["record_name"] == record_name end)
  |> Enum.sort_by(fn f -> String.to_integer(f["field_order"]) end)

field_rows =
  Enum.map_join(this_record_fields, "\n", fn f ->
    required = if f["field_required"] == "true", do: "yes", else: "no"
    "| `#{f["field_name"]}` | `#{f["field_type"]}` | #{required} | #{f["field_doc"]} |"
  end)
%># <%= record_name %>

*Part of the [beam4pm types reference](../beam4pm_types_reference.md). GENERATED by ggen_igniter -- do not edit.*

<%= record_doc %>

## Fields

| Field | Type | Required | Doc |
|---|---|---|---|
<%= field_rows %>

## Constructors

Each of beam4pm's four language projections exposes a `new_<%= record_name %>/1` (or
language-equivalent) validating constructor over this record's admitted field set:

- Erlang: `beam4pm_types:new_<%= record_name %>/1` (`src/beam4pm_types.erl`)
- Elixir: `BeamPM.Types.new_<%= record_name %>/1` (`lib/beam4pm_types.ex`)
- Gleam: `beam4pm/types.new_<%= record_name %>` (`gleam/src/beam4pm/types.gleam`)
- JSON Schema: `<%= record_name %>` definition (`schema/beam4pm_types.schema.json`)

Every constructor returns `{ok, Record}` on success or `{error, {missing_field, Field}}`
for the first missing required field, in field-order.
